{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (an automated orchestrator) assigned task #5635: create differential tests for `cmd/pee` (a moreutils utility that tees stdin to multiple pipe commands). The task specifically requires implementing tests per srd113-pee R2.1 (exit code behavior) and R2.2 (SIGPIPE handling). The deliverable is `cmd/pee/pee_test.go` containing differential tests that compare the Go pee binary against the Homebrew moreutils reference binary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: build Go binary, find reference binary via `exec.LookPath`, run both with identical inputs, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - moreutils reference binaries have NO g-prefix (unlike GNU coreutils which use `gcat`, `gls`, etc.) — the reference binary is just `pee`\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` is the harness that executes both binaries and compares outputs\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd/ package under test\n   - `testutils.NormalizeFunc` for transforming output before comparison (needed because pee output is interleaved/non-deterministic)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - pee executes commands via `sh -c COMMAND`, reads all stdin, fans out to command stdin pipes in parallel\n   - Output from multiple commands is interleaved (non-deterministic order), requiring sort-based normalization\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd113-pee.yaml`\n     - Defines the SRD for pee utility\n     - R1: Pipe teeing (R1.1: accept commands, pipe stdin; R1.2: wait for all; R1.3: stdout interleaved)\n     - R2: Exit codes and SIGPIPE (R2.1: exit 0 when all succeed, exit 1 when any fails; R2.2: SIGPIPE handling)\n     - Non-goals