e\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\n\"), ExitCode: 1},\n             {Name: \"mixed_exit_codes\", Args: []string{\"true\", \"false\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\n\"), ExitCode: 1, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{sortLines}},\n             {Name: \"empty_stdin\", Args: []string{\"cat\"}, Stdin: []byte{}},\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n\n     func TestSIGPIPE(t *testing.T) { ... }\n     ```\n     - 7 DiffTest entries covering: no arguments, single command, multiple commands with normalization, three commands, failing command (R2.1), mixed exit codes (R2.1), empty stdin (R2.2 edge case)\n     - TestSIGPIPE covers R2.2\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The file was read but no build/test commands were executed.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Discovery: The file `cmd/pee/pee_test.go` already exists with what appears to be a complete implementation. This was discovered when reading the file (it returned content instead of a \"file not found\" error).\n   - The existing implementation appears to cover all acceptance criteria, but this has not been verified by running `go vet` or `go test`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Single massive task message containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), task description with required reading/files/requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, execution constitution, go style constitution, shared protocols, package contracts, and constraints.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify `cmd/pee/pee_test.go` compiles: `go vet ./cmd/pee/...`\n   - Run tests: `go test ./cmd/pee/... -count=1`\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria are met (AC1-AC5)\n   - Determine if any test cases are missing per srd113-pee R2.1 and R2.2\n   - If the file already fully satisfies requirements, confirm completion\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four required fi